i) Cash before Shipment/Cash at Shipment;

ii) Irrevocable Letters of Credit

iii) Export Credit Insurance (for comprehensive commercial and political

risk);

iv) Collections (Cash against Documents); and

v) Open Account;

c) Credit insurance experience;

d) The composition and quality of the collateral in the proposed borrowing base that may include:

i) Quality of the Borrower’s customer base;

ii) The presence of concentrations risks;

iii) Delinquency volumes and trends; and

iv) Dilution.

xii. A discussion of Lender’s credit experience with the Applicant and a review

of business and personal credit reports.

d. Collateral

See Section A, Ch. 5, Para. A. for guaranty requirements.

